{"title":"2025 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Faster)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Faster)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Using_Symmetry)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Using Symmetry)</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A standard six-sided die will be rolled two times. What is the probability that the outcome of the second roll will be greater than the outcome of the first roll?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/e/28e24c43456d95b5ab8d4f2f8f85a644e98b7ed3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a, b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> represent the combination of rolls where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is the first roll and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is the second roll. Listing all of the possibilities, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/f/31fa6b94e5a84b15c9a080cd52edc749580d90c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/2/69273482bff8727194f6407e55ac1bfa94d9c555.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/a/1ba3e3f9bd99ddc2bf9e6d9244ebf4bfbc3776d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/1/5a1acbf245a710398f64953985490d7b1134630b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/b/dbb8858b7eefd40608ac2c33f75f1c80b800bc74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/d/d5df99ccd1c7c4b384bb2b3a5b9d270c6aa4abf0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/a/f7a25c234892fb8a7738bc31e5ccee3bf9ad5afc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/0/5506b58320deb5004bf2ed2f1a5e3e672d6e326e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/a/68a601c8e837eafe7d899c2ba96295b3637daf6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2, 3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/6/4c6f0e4cd615eb4d118bf243be6594935ad3de9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2, 4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/c/20c86ca1c4b2e0ef486c0cafcf9a2eefffa10421.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2, 5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/f/70f47290d3c991aac723270e49b5415eb82b2cc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2, 6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/6/d261236ea904095d8d185a456444545b5206013b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/4/ea44bd62795a5d84c16a028ff4fb079a5cb8e63f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/4/c04fa1d70044a676ae0a28e1476d5192f5cd8496.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3, 3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/c/dcc1c720139325a2c3491ba41476d225311fcd1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3, 4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/9/9492e0ae17ba8045ad2de885400cf91207e83db5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3, 5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/1/281cb98ef359560b94673052664a637c131ec362.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3, 6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/5/78561eb59286ee78766fdc37ef35399bf0355e7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1924ac42c8e1d1cb79000224acbe2c46d4b22bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/4/7347741cade420c9172f1251847efddfdeb489ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4, 3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/a/79ad99fd4eff7c80182e09559fe59f36b5844e2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4, 4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/1/6b148ef6cc1c0ce3aebeede22fd06969a213bd5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4, 5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/0/190d53edddf17fdf15d88488290c282a150354d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4, 6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/5/2e5c05123d72c760159fe732b683014c75008c17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/e/53e45c55a387ecd0ff1c5c07aa081bdcd9a7fbbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/1/ba1cf8a9e18c3e06c87c6bb9840782dc4c7828a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5, 3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/9/bf953fb2c072b3fd3f9daad973c7e1ee5fc53aff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5, 4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/b/c4b6a364920ec84c82c57831adffe0e2ad2b9be6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5, 5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/b/f2b5a7c6dea205547307d7f8a9f35366c15b819d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5, 6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/0/5a0994ca0283f051e07f29844f7af73f4624eef1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(6, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/7/c17384a6c2a4aee0ea47051a974ad1cb5967d47f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(6, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/3/e936447969453c86785fddfee03c502514fa298f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(6, 3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/a/50a6aa4fae2c4e4c29b43f57a15cd214e525e111.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(6, 4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/2/0429617bc1afa148bd90f2912e2e3f0a85c98ec1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(6, 5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/d/0dd1499dbb1ea032542c13537a2ca2f157d4c832.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(6, 6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Counting, we see that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce5d3cbb9ab0a992ed503c2d4499e4f4af2f9d65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> possibilities for the rolls and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> of them are ways that the second roll can be larger than the first roll.\n</p><p>Thus, the probability of the second roll being larger than the first roll would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/6/676f2ed7502f855f38d57378d8e381ffacffcc4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{15}{36} = \\boxed{\\frac{5}{12}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"82\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Faster.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Faster)\">Solution 2 (Faster)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Faster)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since each die has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> sides, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/7/897dd68f9e342665851f9e9b91b87a28d42fc7e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 \\times 6 = 36$\" width=\"82\" height=\"12\" /> possibilities for the two rolls in total.\n</p><p>If the first roll is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and the first roll is smaller than the second roll, then the second die roll can go from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/8/498538e0c5e486e73a341926ae724fdff91776ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 - 2 + 1 = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" />. From this, we also realise that the number of ways decreases by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> each time the first roll is increased by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> because the lower number that the second die roll can be increases by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> each time as well, so the total number of ways is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/0/680431e5b1d91f746d6a12178bb205c9b8f8aa9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 + 4 + 3 + 2 + 1 + 0 = 9 + 6 = 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"275\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, the probability of the second roll being larger than the first roll would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/6/676f2ed7502f855f38d57378d8e381ffacffcc4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{15}{36} = \\boxed{\\frac{5}{12}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"82\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Using_Symmetry.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Using_Symmetry)\">Solution 3 (Using Symmetry)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Using Symmetry)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since each die has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> sides, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/7/897dd68f9e342665851f9e9b91b87a28d42fc7e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 \\times 6 = 36$\" width=\"82\" height=\"12\" /> possibilities for the two rolls in total. This also means that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ways for the two dies to have the same rolls, meaning that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/2/4028e4e459cafdcae55791faeb09a518a6506a8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36 - 6 = 30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" /> ways for the rolls to be different, or a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/1/f61c1126a0df7bc1bc49cf091defc0c42f60fc50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{30}{36} = \\frac{5}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"61\" height=\"38\" /> probability of the rolls being different.\n</p><p>We then realise that the probability that the first roll is greater than the second roll is the same as the probability that the second roll is greater than the first roll based on symmetry.\n</p><p>Thus, the probability of the second roll being larger than the first roll would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/b/feba73d7523e4b41b68449cd7c2346a1d3918bbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{6} \\div 2 = \\boxed{\\frac{5}{12}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"104\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CSMC\" title=\"2025 CSMC\">2025 CSMC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CSMC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CSMC Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CSMC_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CSMC Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_2\" title=\"2025 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 2\">Part A Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_4\" title=\"2025 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 4\">Part A Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_1\" title=\"2025 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 1\">Part A 1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_2\" title=\"2025 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 2\">Part A 2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Part A 3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_4\" title=\"2025 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 4\">Part A 4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">Part A 5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">Part A 6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1\" title=\"2025 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 1\">Part B 1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 2 (page does not exist)\">Part B 2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 3 (page does not exist)\">Part B 3</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=CEMC_Senior_Competition\" title=\"CEMC Senior Competition\">CEMC Senior Competition</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018070414\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.035 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.055 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 349/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1283/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 134/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 10446/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.997      1 Template:CEMC_CIMC/CSMC_box\n100.00%    6.997      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:37469:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018070414 and revision id 289506. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}